{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "LEV",
  "chapter": 14,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This shall be the law of the leper in the day of his cleansing: He shall be brought to the priest:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall go forth out of the camp: and the priest shall look, and behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the plague of leprosy is healed in the leper;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shall the priest command to take for him that is to be cleansed two birds alive, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " clean, and cedar-wood, and scarlet, and hyssop.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall command that one of the birds be killed in an earthen vessel, over running water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for the living bird, he shall take it, and the cedar-wood, and the scarlet, and the hyssop, and shall dip them, and the living bird, in the blood of the bird ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " killed over the running water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall sprinkle upon him that is to be cleansed from the leprosy seven times, and shall pronounce him clean, and shall let the living bird loose into the open field.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he that is to be cleansed shall wash his clothes, and shave off all his hair, and wash himself in water, that he may be clean: and after that he shall come into the camp, and shall tarry abroad out of his tent seven days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But it shall be on the seventh day, that he shall shave all his hair off his head, and his beard, and his eye-brows, even all his hair he shall shave off; and he shall wash his clothes, also he shall wash his flesh in water, and he shall be clean.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And on the eighth day he shall take two he-lambs without blemish, and one ewe-lamb of the first year without blemish, and three tenth-parts of fine flour ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a meat-offering, mingled with oil, and one log of oil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest that maketh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " clean, shall present the man that is to be made clean, and those things, before the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "at",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall take one he-lamb, and offer him for a trespass-offering, and the log of oil, and wave them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wave-offering before the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall slay the lamb in the place where he shall kill the sin-offering and the burnt-offering, in the holy-place: for as the sin-offering ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the priest's, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the trespass-offering: it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " most holy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the blood of the trespass-offering, and the priest shall put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the log of oil, and pour ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
