      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall offer the burnt-offering, and the meat-offering upon the altar: and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and he shall be clean.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " poor, and cannot get so much; then he shall take one lamb ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a trespass-offering to be waved, to make an atonement for him, and one tenth-part of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat-offering, and a log of oil;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And two turtle-doves, or two young pigeons, such as he is able to get; and the one shall be a sin-offering, and the other a burnt-offering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall bring them on the eighth day for his cleansing to the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, before the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
