    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When ye shall have come into the land of Canaan, which I give to you for a possession, and I put the plague of leprosy in a house of the land of your possession;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he that owneth the house shall come and tell the priest, saying, it seemeth to me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as it were a plague in the house:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the priest shall command that they empty the house, before the priest shall enter to see the plague, that all that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the house may not be made unclean; and afterward the priest shall go in to see the house:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall look on the plague, and behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the plague ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the walls of the house, with hollow streaks, greenish, or reddish, which in sight ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lower than the wall;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the priest shall go out of the house to the door of the house, and shut up the house seven days:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall look; and behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the plague is spread in the walls of the house;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the priest shall command that they take away the stones in which the plague ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and they shall cast them into an unclean place without the city:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall cause the house to be scraped within on all sides, and they shall pour out the dust that they scrape off without the city into an unclean place:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they shall take other stones, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the place of those stones; and he shall take other mortar, and shall plaster the house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LEV.14.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LEV.14.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if the plague shall return, and break out in the house, after that he hath taken away the stones, and after he hath scraped the house, and after it is plastered;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
